experiment: ctxfactor
  instrument        ctxfactor   trial seed 0000000001355b7a   2428 trials per arm
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)
  ctxfactor -- is the learned FOUR-CONTEXT table additive in its two
  features? Every context currently owns independent parameters, so the
  creature cannot generalise across them. A FACTORED table would fix that,
  and is only free if what is learned is already additive. This measures it
  on a trained creature, with no new mechanism.
  the split     EXACT for a 2x2: per neuron, a mean plus three ORTHOGONAL
                contrasts -- the F1 feature, the F2 feature, and their
                INTERACTION, which is the part a factored table cannot hold.
  the null      DERIVED: four rows carry one mean and three orthogonal
                contrasts, so independent rows split the context-dependent
                power equally and chance is 1/3. Additivity is BELOW that.
  the bar       the interaction share sits below 1/3 by 3 SE on the ORACLE
                arm. The SIZE is reported separately, because 0.10 and 0.30
                are both passes and only one is worth building.
  void if       the context-INDEPENDENT part dominates: then the table
                hardly distinguishes contexts and the split is noise.

